# The build context is the project root (deploy/Dockerfile needs `api/` and `web/` side
# by side), which means every line below is something that would otherwise be sent to
# the daemon and baked into an image that then leaves this machine.
#
# The two that matter are not about size:
#
#   api/storage   every profile photo students have uploaded
#   api/backups   a complete copy of the database, plus those same photos
#
# A photo of a student, and a dump of who messaged whom, do not belong in a Docker image
# that someone might push to a registry. They stay on the server, in a volume, and the
# backup script writes them somewhere the server is not.
#
# What is deliberately *not* here: `web/`. Both stages build from the real sources —
# stage 1 compiles the site with vite, so ignoring any part of web/ would fail the build
# rather than slim the image.

# ---- dependencies and build output: regenerated inside the image --------------
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/

# ---- secrets and personal data -----------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/prod.env
api/storage/
api/backups/
api/outbox/
outbox/
storage/

# ---- things the running container never reads --------------------------------
.git/
PLAN/
api/test/
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
.DS_Store
